{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1485","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Copy or Prefix Sum"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array of integers $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An array $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ of integers is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"hybrid"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if for each $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\leq i \\leq n$$$) at least one of these conditions is true: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$b_i = a_i$$$, or "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$b_i = \\sum_{j=1}^{i} a_j$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the number of hybrid arrays $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$. As the result can be very large, you should print the answer modulo $$$10^9 + 7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_n$$$ ($$$-10^9 \\le b_i \\le 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ for all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a single integer: the number of hybrid arrays $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ modulo $$$10^9 + 7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n3\n1 -1 1\n4\n1 2 3 4\n10\n2 -1 1 -2 2 3 -5 0 2 -1\n4\n0 0 0 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n8\n223\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the hybrid arrays are $$$[1, -2, 1]$$$, $$$[1, -2, 2]$$$, $$$[1, -1, 1]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, the hybrid arrays are $$$[1, 1, 1, 1]$$$, $$$[1, 1, 1, 4]$$$, $$$[1, 1, 3, -1]$$$, $$$[1, 1, 3, 4]$$$, $$$[1, 2, 0, 1]$$$, $$$[1, 2, 0, 4]$$$, $$$[1, 2, 3, -2]$$$, $$$[1, 2, 3, 4]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth test case, the only hybrid array is $$$[0, 0, 0, 1]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1485F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1485/problem/F"}